From: Clover Windows lane <clover@example.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Per-principal setup records plus a --user selector

---







Upstream: anthropics/sandbox-runtime, tag v0.0.81 (c40cf14).
Reason: one machine-global setup record means only the last install
can launch (`exec` exit 15 otherwise) and an `uninstall` orphans the
other installs' records. Clover runs one sandbox principal per
session from a small per-user pool, so each install needs its own
record and every launch path needs to name which principal it means.

What changes, and nothing else:
- HKLM\SOFTWARE\sandbox-runtime\Users\<principal>\ carries the
  same identity values as the global record (SandboxUser,
  SandboxUserSid, SandboxGroupSid, MarkerVersion, CreatedAt) plus
  the install's SublayerGuid, and Cred\<principal>\Blob carries
  that install's DPAPI credential. The global record keeps its
  exact current semantics (last install wins) so unpatched
  readers are unaffected; the `--user` selectors read here.
- install::read_setup_for / require_current_setup_for /
  read_cred_for take an optional principal; the old fns keep their
  signatures as the global (None) case.
- `exec --user <principal>` and `user status --user <principal>`
  launch against / report that principal's record. Without the flag
  the behavior is byte-for-byte the old behavior.
- `uninstall --user <principal>` removes only that principal's
  Users subkey, Cred blob and account, plus the WFP filters under
  --sublayer as before. The global record is removed only when it
  names that principal.

Upstream-ready: the global record is untouched, all new behavior is
opt-in behind --user, and the default `srt-sandbox` flow is unchanged.

